      "message": "fix(post): grblHAL lifts Z in the work offset unless the machine homes\n\nWithout homing ($22=0) grblHAL takes its power-on position as machine\nzero, so the G53 G0 Z0 lift before each tool change and at the end could\nrapid down into the part. The post now writes G53 G0 Z<safe> only when\nthe machine file states safe_retract (the statement that it homes);\notherwise it lifts with G0 Z<h> in the work offset, h the section's\nClearancePlane or a higher Z the program already commanded, refused by\nname when h is unknown or not above StockZTop. The generic grblHAL\nmachine no longer states safe_retract.\n\nRefs #710\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
